import{_ as i,o as a,c as t,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 444 | Dragon Ball · Dragon Balls Setting Critique: Causal Disruption of Arbitrary Wishing","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 444 | Dragon Ball · Dragon Balls Setting Critique: Causal Disruption of Arbitrary Wishing","no":444,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Dragon Ball Wish","Causal Disruption","Causal Self-Discipline Axiom","Historical Regression"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0444_模块2-龙珠-龙珠设定批判-随意许愿的因果扰乱.md","filePath":"en/0444_模块2-龙珠-龙珠设定批判-随意许愿的因果扰乱.md"}'),o={name:"en/0444_模块2-龙珠-龙珠设定批判-随意许愿的因果扰乱.md"};function r(n,e,l,h,d,u){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-444-dragon-ball-·-dragon-balls-setting-critique-causal-disruption-of-arbitrary-wishing" tabindex="-1">Entry 444 | Dragon Ball · Dragon Balls Setting Critique: Causal Disruption of Arbitrary Wishing <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-444-dragon-ball-·-dragon-balls-setting-critique-causal-disruption-of-arbitrary-wishing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 444 | Dragon Ball · Dragon Balls Setting Critique: Causal Disruption of Arbitrary Wishing&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 13) | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 49, 03</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-wishes-have-no-threshold" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when wishes have no threshold <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-wishes-have-no-threshold" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when wishes have no threshold&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Balls themselves are this IP&#39;s name, also its most dangerous setting: seven balls gathered, summon the dragon god, grant any wish — revive people, exterminate a race, make someone young again, make the dead die again, restore the universe. No threshold, no review, no price (early &quot;one-year lifespan&quot; later also broken). This entry takes the <strong>causal self-discipline axiom</strong> as core, dissecting how &quot;arbitrary wishing&quot; thoroughly disrupts Dragon Ball world&#39;s causality.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The wishing mechanism itself is energy waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Revival = history zeroed</strong>: every wish to revive the dead erases civilization&#39;s trauma memory; history does not advance</li><li><strong>Wish = resource allocation</strong>: whoever gathers the balls takes the biggest cosmos-tier resource — this is naked resource competition, unrelated to cultivation</li><li><strong>Dragon god&#39;s public resource privatized</strong>: the dragon god should have been Myriad Ranks&#39; public miracle, yet privately used by whoever gathers the balls — this public resource repeatedly diverted to private wishes</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How the wishing mechanism feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Causality arbitrarily modified</strong>: dead can revive, cities can restore, time can reverse — civilization&#39;s law of causality is hollowed out by Dragon Balls</li><li><strong>Effort loses meaning</strong>: since can wish revival, why cherish life? Since can wish restore, why build cities?</li><li><strong>Wish = power</strong>: whoever gathers Dragon Balls has power to rewrite reality — this power does not rely on cultivation, contribution, legislation, only on &quot;gather seven balls&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking in the wishing mechanism:</p><ul><li><strong>Revival resource repeatedly used</strong>: Goku&#39;s party repeatedly gathers Dragon Balls to &quot;revive companions&quot;; this &quot;revival right&quot; used by them as public resource — but Frieza, Cell, Buu also wished back, proving this mechanism is not controlled by Goku at all</li><li><strong>Wish = shortcut to solve problems</strong>: after beating Buu, after beating Zamasu, after beating Jiren, it always ends &quot;wish restore everything&quot; — Goku never truly solves problems, just erases problems by wish</li><li><strong>No reverence for causality</strong>: Goku never reflects &quot;did reviving these people disrupt causality&quot; — he treats the dragon god as a tool person, uses it when he wants</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Arbitrary Wishing</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Causal Self-Discipline Plan</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gather then wish</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: cross-plane operations strictly filed; observe first then limited interference</td></tr><tr><td>Revival no threshold</td><td>Revival goes Symbiotic Court approval: who revives, why, what price</td></tr><tr><td>Wish = power</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism: any reality-rewriting operation goes Anchor Council legislation</td></tr><tr><td>History erased</td><td>Civilization trauma memory retained; revival does not rewrite history</td></tr><tr><td>Dragon god as tool person</td><td>Dragon-god-tier power under Alaya supervision; not diverted by any private party</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball wishing history — revive companions, revive Frieza, restore Earth, restore universe</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if wishing needs causal self-discipline approval; revival goes Symbiotic Court&quot; control</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Dragon Balls privately diverted times, civilization trauma memory retention rate, law-of-causality modified times</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Wish Causal-Disruption Report</em>, quantifying &quot;every wish devalues how much Dragon Ball world&#39;s law of causality&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. Earth Dragon Balls (one wish, one-year lifespan) → Namekian Dragon Balls (three wishes) → Super Dragon Balls (cross-universe wishes) → Black Star Dragon Balls (planet explodes after wish); rules added with plot</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. Revival rules repeatedly changed between original, GT, Super; Cell, Frieza, Buu&#39;s revival conditions inconsistent</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Goku&#39;s party is Dragon Balls&#39; main user; Myriad Ranks gather Dragon Balls far less</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: wishing zeroes history, invalidates effort, erases trauma memory</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: public miracle privately diverted; revival right repeatedly used by Goku&#39;s party</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least raised cultivation by effort; Goku solves problems by wishing</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: among Myriad Ranks only those who gather Dragon Balls can use the dragon god; the vast majority of beings have no access</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: wishing mechanism lets law of causality thoroughly collapse; cannot expand to stable multiverse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Dragon Balls wishing mechanism is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s most charming and most dangerous design — it realized childhood wishes, also hollowed out civilization&#39;s law of causality. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the causal self-discipline axiom: any reality-rewriting operation must be filed, approved, trail-marked; revival is not forbidden, but must go legal process, must retain trauma memory, must let Myriad-Ranks parliament know. Let the dragon god return to &quot;Myriad Ranks&#39; public miracle&quot; position, not a wish machine for whoever gathers the balls — this is the true way out for Dragon Balls&#39; wishing mechanism.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Dragon Balls setting critique · causal disruption of arbitrary wishing described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./466_模块2-龙珠-因果自律缺失-龙珠许愿与因果扰乱.html">Entry 466 · Causal Self-Discipline Absence</a> · <a href="./432_模块2-龙珠-总论悟空与战力膨胀体系定性.html">Entry 432 · Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
